<title>USA: Hyperion sets IPO price range at $1! to $13.</title>
<headline>Hyperion sets IPO price range at $1! to $13.</headline>
<dateline>COUDERSPORT, Pa. 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hyperion Telecommunications Inc on Friday set terms of its proposed initial public offering at 16.5 million Class A shares to be sold in an estimated range of $11 to $13 each.</p>
<p>Hyperion is a subsidiary of Adelphia Communications Corp, which currently holds 17,800,040 shares of Hyperion's Class B common stock, as adjusted for the IPO, or about 89 percent of the common stock outstanding.</p>
<p>The Class B common stock of Hyperion is convertible into Class A common stock on a one-to-one basis, it said.</p>
</text>
